Skip TracePoint under Opal, which has none; symbol imports resolve lazily.
Temporary: from lutaml/lutaml-model branch fix/opal-runtime-compat (77cefafb);
remove once that branch is released and LUTAML_MODEL_REF moves past it.

diff --git a/lib/lutaml/model/serialize/model_import.rb b/lib/lutaml/model/serialize/model_import.rb
index 8c4e809f..7660518b 100644
--- a/lib/lutaml/model/serialize/model_import.rb
+++ b/lib/lutaml/model/serialize/model_import.rb
@@ -243,6 +243,11 @@ module Lutaml
         # Uses TracePoint to detect when a class definition is complete,
         # allowing deferred import resolution.
         def setup_trace_point
+          # Opal has no TracePoint. Symbol imports still resolve lazily
+          # on first use (ensure_imports!), so there the class is marked
+          # finalized at once instead of at the end of its body.
+          return @finalized = true if Lutaml::Model.opal?
+
           @trace ||= TracePoint.new(:end) do |_tp|
             if include?(Lutaml::Model::Serialize)
               @finalized = true
